<spell-page "utilities" notebook>
	<header level="1">
		Utilities
		<header>Token-driven layout, sizing, text, colour and visibility classes, on your markup and inside components.</>
	</>

	<!--
		UTILITIES:  the old `utilities.mdx` (our own:  Fomantic has no utilities page), section by section.
		- The utilities are CLASSES for your own markup, so the examples are plain `<div class="ui-...">`s:  the subject,
		  not page chrome.  The boxes they arrange are utility-drawn placeholders too.
		- `style=` only where the utility's own knob IS a custom property (`--min-column-size`, `--content-percentage`).
	-->
	<section label="Overview">
		<markdown>
			Every utility is a `ui-*` class in `@layer ui.utilities`, injected into the page AND adopted into every shadow
			root, so it works on your markup and inside components alike. Lengths come from the spacing tokens (`em` of the
			local font size), so utilities scale with their region. Modifiers use an escaped colon (`ui-split:column`, written
			`.ui-split\:column` in CSS), fractions an escaped slash (`ui-w-1/2`).

			- `<space>` is `3xs 2xs xs s m l xl 2xl 3xl`.
			- `<size>` is `mini tiny small medium large big huge massive`.
			- The pale blue boxes below are placeholders, themselves drawn with utilities (`ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-s`).
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Layout">
		<section label="Stack" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Stack" description="`ui-stack`:  children in a column with even gaps;  their own block margins are dropped.">
				<stack class="ui-stack">
					<stack class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-s">One</stack>
					<stack class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-s">Two</stack>
					<stack class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-s">Three</stack>
				</stack>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Cluster" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Cluster" description="`ui-cluster`:  inline items that wrap, e.g. tags or buttons.">
				<stack class="ui-cluster">
					<text class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-s">Alpha</text>
					<text class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-s">Bravo</text>
					<text class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-s">Charlie</text>
					<text class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-s">Delta</text>
					<text class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-s">Echo</text>
				</stack>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Split" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Split" description="`ui-split`:  push items to opposite ends;  `ui-split:column` / `ui-split:row` fix the direction.">
				<stack class="ui-split">
					<text class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-s">Start</text>
					<text class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-s">End</text>
				</stack>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Flank" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Flank" description="`ui-flank`:  a fixed-size item beside flexible content, wrapping when the content gets narrower than `--content-percentage` (70%).  `ui-flank:end` flanks the last child.">
				<stack class="ui-flank">
					<text class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-s">Flank</text>
					<stack class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-s">Flexible content takes the rest of the row.</stack>
				</stack>
				<stack class="ui-flank ui-flank:end">
					<stack class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-s">Flexible content first, the flank at the end.</stack>
					<text class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-s">Flank</text>
				</stack>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Frame" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Frame" description="`ui-frame`:  a fixed aspect ratio, media inside covers it;  `ui-frame:square`, `:landscape`, `:portrait`.">
				<stack class="ui-cluster ui-align-items-start">
					<stack class="ui-frame ui-frame:square ui-bg-blue ui-w-1/4">square</stack>
					<stack class="ui-frame ui-frame:landscape ui-bg-green ui-w-1/3">landscape</stack>
					<stack class="ui-frame ui-frame:portrait ui-bg-violet ui-w-1/4">portrait</stack>
				</stack>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Grid" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Grid" description="`ui-grid`:  as many columns as fit, each at least `--min-column-size` (default `20ch`);  `ui-span-grid` spans a full row.">
				<stack style="--min-column-size: 8em" class="ui-grid">
					<stack class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-s">1</stack>
					<stack class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-s">2</stack>
					<stack class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-s">3</stack>
					<stack class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-s">4</stack>
					<stack class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-s ui-span-grid">ui-span-grid</stack>
				</stack>
			</example>
		</>

		<!-- SUSPECTED BUG (agents/SUSPECTED-BUGS.md, ui):  `ui-gap-*` loses to the layout primitives' own `gap` (same specificity, earlier in the sheet), so these rows are `ui-flex`, not `ui-cluster`. -->
		<section label="Gap" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Gap" description="`ui-gap-<space>` sets the gap of a flex or grid container;  `ui-gap-0` removes it.">
				<stack class="ui-stack ui-gap-s">
					<stack class="ui-flex ui-gap-3xs">
						<text class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-s">3xs</text>
						<text class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-s">3xs</text>
					</stack>
					<stack class="ui-flex ui-gap-m">
						<text class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-s">m</text>
						<text class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-s">m</text>
					</stack>
					<stack class="ui-flex ui-gap-2xl">
						<text class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-s">2xl</text>
						<text class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-s">2xl</text>
					</stack>
				</stack>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Align and justify" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Align and justify" description="`ui-align-items-*`, `ui-align-self-*`, `ui-justify-content-*`, `ui-flex-wrap` / `-nowrap`.">
				<stack class="ui-flex ui-align-items-end ui-justify-content-space-between ui-gap-s">
					<stack class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-l ui-rounded-s">tall box</stack>
					<text class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-s ui-align-self-center">self center</text>
					<text class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-s">end</text>
				</stack>
			</example>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Sizing">
		<section label="Widths" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Widths" description="`ui-w-1/2`, `1/3`, `2/3`, `1/4`, `3/4`, `full`, `auto`, `fit`;  `ui-h-full`, `auto`, `fit`.">
				<stack class="ui-stack ui-gap-xs">
					<stack class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-s ui-w-1/4">ui-w-1/4</stack>
					<stack class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-s ui-w-1/2">ui-w-1/2</stack>
					<stack class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-s ui-w-3/4">ui-w-3/4</stack>
					<stack class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-s ui-w-fit">ui-w-fit</stack>
				</stack>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Margin and padding" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Margin and padding" description="`ui-m\[-side]-<space>` and `ui-p\[-side]-<space>`, logical sides `b i bs be is ie`.">
				<stack class="ui-cluster ui-align-items-start">
					<stack class="ui-bg-grey ui-p-2xs">ui-p-2xs</stack>
					<stack class="ui-bg-grey ui-p-l">ui-p-l</stack>
					<stack class="ui-bg-grey ui-p-i-xl">ui-p-i-xl</stack>
					<stack class="ui-bg-grey ui-m-bs-l">ui-m-bs-l</stack>
				</stack>
			</example>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Text">
		<section label="Roles" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Roles" description="`ui-body`, `ui-heading`, `ui-caption`, each with sized variants (`ui-heading-large` ...).">
				<stack class="ui-stack ui-gap-2xs">
					<text class="ui-heading ui-m-0" paragraph>ui-heading</text>
					<text class="ui-heading-small ui-m-0" paragraph>ui-heading-small</text>
					<text class="ui-body ui-m-0" paragraph>ui-body: the running text of a page.</text>
					<text class="ui-caption ui-m-0" paragraph>ui-caption: smaller and muted.</text>
				</stack>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Size and weight" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Size and weight" description="`ui-font-size-<size>`, `ui-font-weight-{light,normal,semibold,bold}`, `ui-bold`, `ui-italic`, `ui-muted`.">
				<stack class="ui-cluster ui-align-items-baseline">
					<text class="ui-font-size-tiny">tiny</text>
					<text class="ui-font-size-large">large</text>
					<text class="ui-font-size-huge">huge</text>
					<text class="ui-font-weight-light">light</text>
					<text class="ui-font-weight-semibold">semibold</text>
					<text class="ui-bold">bold</text>
					<text class="ui-italic">italic</text>
					<text class="ui-muted">muted</text>
				</stack>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Alignment and wrapping" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Alignment and wrapping" description="`ui-text-{start,center,end,justify}`, `ui-text-{nowrap,balance,pretty,truncate}`, `ui-text-{uppercase,lowercase,capitalize}`.">
				<stack class="ui-stack ui-gap-xs">
					<text class="ui-text-center ui-m-0" paragraph>ui-text-center</text>
					<text class="ui-text-end ui-m-0" paragraph>ui-text-end</text>
					<text class="ui-text-truncate ui-w-1/2 ui-m-0" paragraph>ui-text-truncate cuts a long line off with an ellipsis instead of wrapping it onto the next line</text>
					<text class="ui-text-uppercase ui-m-0" paragraph>ui-text-uppercase</text>
				</stack>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Links and lists" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Links and lists" description="`ui-link`, `ui-link-plain` (underline on hover only), `ui-list-plain`, `ui-selectable` (text to read and copy, in a page that is an app:  `<ui-root app>`), `ui-content-size` (what such an app shows, at the theme's own sizes, where the theme gives an app smaller ones).">
				<stack class="ui-stack ui-gap-xs">
					<text class="ui-m-0" paragraph><link link="#links-and-lists" class="ui-link">ui-link</link> and <link link="#links-and-lists" class="ui-link-plain">ui-link-plain</link></text>
					<list role="list" class="ui-list-plain ui-m-0" bulleted>
						<item>ui-list-plain</item>
						<item>no bullets, no indent</item>
					</list>
				</stack>
			</example>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Colour">
		<section label="Colour roles" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Colour roles" description="`ui-text-<colour>`, `ui-bg-<colour>` (the pale background role), `ui-border-<colour>` (with a border width of your own).">
				<stack class="ui-cluster">
					<text class="ui-text-red">ui-text-red</text>
					<text class="ui-bg-green ui-p-2xs">ui-bg-green</text>
					<text class="ui-text-violet ui-bg-violet ui-p-2xs ui-rounded-s">ui-text-violet ui-bg-violet</text>
					<text class="ui-text-orange ui-bg-orange ui-p-2xs ui-rounded-s">ui-text-orange ui-bg-orange</text>
				</stack>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Remap" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Remap" description="`ui-<hue>` re-points the generic `--ui-color` tokens, so it recolours the uncoloured components inside a wrapper that take a colour (buttons, checkboxes, progress bars ...).">
				<stack class="ui-teal ui-cluster">
					<button>Button</button>
					<progress value="40" class="ui-w-1/3" aria-label="Progress"/>
					<checkbox selected>Checkbox</checkbox>
				</stack>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Scheme" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Scheme" description="`ui-light`, `ui-dark` force a scheme on a subtree;  `ui-invert` flips relative to its parent.">
				<stack class="ui-cluster">
					<segment class="ui-light">ui-light</segment>
					<segment class="ui-dark">ui-dark <segment class="ui-invert">ui-invert</segment></segment>
				</stack>
			</example>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Shape">
		<section label="Rounding" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Rounding" description="`ui-rounded-{s,m,l,pill,circle,square}`.">
				<stack class="ui-cluster">
					<stack class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-square">square</stack>
					<stack class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-s">s</stack>
					<stack class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-m">m</stack>
					<stack class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-l">l</stack>
					<stack class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-pill">pill</stack>
					<stack class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-circle ui-frame ui-frame:square">circle</stack>
				</stack>
			</example>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Misc">
		<section label="Prose" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Prose" description="`ui-prose`:  readable rich text (a line measure plus vertical rhythm);  `ui-not-prose` opts a subtree back out.">
				<html>
					<ui-stack class="ui-prose">
						<h3>A heading</h3>
						<ui-text paragraph>Paragraphs, lists and quotes get a measure and even spacing, so CMS or markdown output reads well.</ui-text>
						<blockquote>A quote, with a rule on its start side.</blockquote>
						<ui-stack class="ui-not-prose">
							<h3>ui-not-prose: untouched</h3>
						</ui-stack>
					</ui-stack>
				</html>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Visually hidden" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Visually hidden" description="`ui-visually-hidden` hides content but keeps it for screen readers, and shows it again when focus moves inside (skip links);  `ui-visually-hidden-force` never shows it.">
				<stack class="ui-cluster">
					<text>Visible text</text>
					<text class="ui-visually-hidden">read by screen readers only</text>
					<link link="#visually-hidden" class="ui-visually-hidden">Tab to me</link>
				</stack>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Cloak" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Cloak" description="`ui-cloak` hides undefined custom elements (FOUCE) until they upgrade, for 2s at most.">
				<stack class="ui-cloak">
					<button color="primary">Shown once defined</button>
				</stack>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Display" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Display" description="`ui-out-of-view`, `ui-block`, `ui-flex`;  `ui-hidden-{mobile,tablet,computer}` hide at a breakpoint (resize the window).">
				<stack class="ui-cluster">
					<text class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-s ui-hidden-mobile">hidden on mobile</text>
					<text class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-s ui-hidden-tablet">hidden on tablet</text>
					<text class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-s ui-hidden-computer">hidden on computer</text>
					<text class="ui-bg-blue ui-p-s ui-rounded-s ui-out-of-view">never shown</text>
				</stack>
			</example>
		</>
	</>
</spell-page>
